[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-press-run-decision :authorize-press-run-operation :proceed-with-press-run :override-safety-officer-judgment :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007223-cloud-itonami-isco-7223-metal-working-machine-tool-setters-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the press run" "proceed with the printing press run" "finalize the press run decision" "authorize the press run operation" "authorize the printing press run" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799007322, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :manufacturing/printing-press-shop-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:worker-verified :shop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7322", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007322: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7322 Printers print-shop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7322\n-- Printers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of the rollout (Wave0/1/2\n100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-6 already landed: construction/metal/\nprecision-craft trades, all agriculture classes, ~36 occupations so\nfar).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7322\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/\nget-occupation \\\"7322\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Printers\" -- confirming the\npremise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was\n`:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics :identity\n:audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed\nat `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7322` (`gh api` 404 confirmed\nbefore scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote\nthe `7322` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nPrinters operate printing presses (offset, digital, flexographic) to\nproduce printed output for a print shop -- real physical-safety stakes\n(rotating-machinery hazards, ink/solvent exposure, paper-handling\ninjury). The controlling constraint for this vertical is that the\nclosed op allowlist must NEVER include any op that directly finalizes\na press-run-execution decision, or overrides a shop safety officer's\njudgment -- those decisions must always be a hard permanent block or\nan always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor is\ndeliberately scoped to SHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY --\nit never operates the printing press itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7223`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7223)\n(Metal Working Machine Tool Setters and Operators: `store`/`advisor`/\n`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set,\nthe closely-related rotating-machinery safety pattern already landed)\n-- cloned and read in full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7322` as an OSS print-shop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for printers, following the\nSAME governed-actor architecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*`\nactor in this fleet: **Pressman Advisor ⊣ PressmanGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **shop scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct press-operation authority** -- it must NEVER be\ndesigned to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\npress-run-execution decision, or any override of a shop safety\nofficer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind escalation --\nthey are structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- job/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/press-time scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a machinery-hazard/ink-exposure\n  concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- ink/paper-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\npress-run-execution decision or a shop-safety-officer-judgment\noverride. These are **structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-press-run-decision` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names five\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`pressman.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-press-run-decision`, `:authorize-press-run-operation`,\n`:proceed-with-press-run`, `:override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`pressman.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-press-run-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-press-run-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-press-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Worker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered worker record (`:no-worker`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the worker is.\n2. **Shop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered print shop (`:no-shop`). Together with check 1, this\n   directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a worker/shop\n   record must be independently verified/registered before any\n   action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the five\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a press\n   run, or overriding a shop safety officer's judgment, is a second\n   HARD, PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of the\n   allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   press-run-execution/safety-override language wherever it appears\n   in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a machinery-hazard/\n  ink-exposure observation -- it never resolves the concern itself,\n  and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard data,\" never \"here\n  is what I recommend doing about shop safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an\n  over-threshold ink/paper-materials order is not itself unsafe,\n  unlike a press-run-execution or safety-officer-override attempt,\n  which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate\n  vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"press\", \"ink\") can accidentally match inside the mock advisor's own\ndefault rationale text for a legitimate proposal, self-blocking the\nactor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk this vertical's own\nvocabulary (a print-shop coordination actor working adjacent to\npress-run scheduling necessarily discusses those concepts to do its\nscheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`pressman.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the press run\",\n\"authorize the press run operation\", \"override the shop safety\nofficer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example\nphrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`pressman.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for worker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for press-time\nchangeover ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer review\") WITHOUT\ncontaining any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development. `pressman.actor-test/holds-a-scope-\nexcluded-op-even-at-high-confidence` additionally exercises the same\ninvariant through the full graph run, confirming a scope-excluded\nproposal never reaches `commit-record!` regardless of disposition\npath.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7322\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7322` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7322`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 22 tests, 47 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-press-run` that is merely\n  gated behind an always-escalate list: rejected outright per the\n  task's explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op\n  still means the *capability* to finalize a press-run-execution\n  decision exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human\n  gate. For a decision this severe (rotating-machinery hazards,\n  ink/solvent exposure, paper-handling injury), the capability itself\n  must not exist. The only op related to shop-safety escalation is\n  `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for human/shop-\n  safety-officer attention and never itself decides, authorizes, or\n  defers a press-run-execution decision for later automatic\n  execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold ink/paper-\n  materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft\n  escalate gate, not a hard block; only the press-run-execution/\n  safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. [\"press\" \"ink\"\n  \"safety\"]): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses press/ink/\n  safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so a\n  bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale text that\n  deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Two separate override-authority ops mirroring house-building's\n  safety-officer/foreman split: the task names only \"a shop safety\n  officer's judgment\" as the authority figure for this vertical, so a\n  single dominant op `:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment` (plus a\n  generic `:override-safety-officer-judgment` variant and matching\n  phrase variants, to defend against either phrasing appearing in an\n  advisor's free text) covers the specified scope without inventing an\n  unspecified second authority role.\n- Merging `worker` and `shop` into a single entity (only checking one\n  provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered worker AND independently-registered shop)\n  matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/shop record must be\n  independently verified/registered before any action\" and the\n  established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with\n  two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- job/materials-usage/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered worker AND shop\n   (`:no-worker`/`:no-shop`). Not a press-run-execution decision in\n   any respect -- it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/press-time scheduling\n   proposal only. Cannot carry a press-run-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   proceeding with a specific printing press run -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a machinery-hazard/\n   ink-exposure concern to a human/shop safety officer; ALWAYS\n   escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the shop safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- ink/paper-materials procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a press-run-execution or\n   authorization decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000\n   always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na press-run-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a specific\nprinting press run) or a shop-safety-officer-judgment override --\nthese categories are structurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a)\nthe closed four-op allowlist itself (`pressman.governor/allowed-ops`),\n(b) five concretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the\ngovernor-unit level (`pressman.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`pressman.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-press-run-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-press-run-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-press-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`pressman.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a press run or override a shop safety\nofficer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`pressman.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 22, :assertions 47, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Print Shop Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :worker-verification :shop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7322", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7322", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7322], :test/simulator :pressman.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7322 — Printers Shop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7322}]